{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-84726","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119100","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-84727","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119101","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119102","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-119103","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-119104","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-119105","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-119106","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-119107","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-119108","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-84728","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-84730","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119109","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-84731","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119110","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-84732","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84734","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119111","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-84733","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84736","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119112","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-84735","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84738","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119113","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-84737","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84740","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119114","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-84739","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119115","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-84741","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119116","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-84743","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119117","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-84745","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119118","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-84747","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119119","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-84749","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84751","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119120","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-84752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119121","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-119122","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-119123","text":". You declare "},{"id":"spn-119124","marks":["italic"],"text":"rooms"},{"id":"spn-119125","text":" (tiles), "},{"id":"spn-119126","marks":["italic"],"text":"claims"},{"id":"spn-119127","text":" (file-system regions each room owns), "},{"id":"spn-119128","marks":["italic"],"text":"neighbors"},{"id":"spn-119129","text":" (adjacency for navigation), and "},{"id":"spn-119130","marks":["italic"],"text":"state bindings"},{"id":"spn-119131","text":" (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-84753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119132","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-119133","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-119134","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-84754","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119135","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-84755","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119136","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-119137","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-119138","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-119139","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-84756","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84759","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119140","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-119141","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-84758","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119142","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-119143","text":" Apps add "},{"id":"spn-119144","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabularies"},{"id":"spn-119145","text":" (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-119146","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-119147","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119148","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-119149","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119150","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-119151","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-84760","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119152","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-119153","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-84762","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84764","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119154","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-84765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119155","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-84766","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119156","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-84767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119157","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-84768","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-84769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119158","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-119159","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119160","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-119161","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-119162","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-119163","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-119164","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-119165","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-84770","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119166","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-84771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119167","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-119168","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-119169","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119170","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-119171","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119172","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-119173","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-84772","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-84773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119174","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-119175","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-119176","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-119177","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-84774","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119178","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-84775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119179","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-119180","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-119181","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-84776","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-84777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119182","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-119183","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-119184","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-119185","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-119186","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-119187","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-119188","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-119189","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-84778","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119190","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-84779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119191","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the "},{"id":"spn-119192","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-119193","text":", not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-84780","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-84781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119194","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-119195","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-119196","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-119197","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119198","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-119199","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119200","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-119201","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119202","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-119203","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119204","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-119205","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-119206","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-119207","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-84782","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119208","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-84783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119209","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-119210","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-119211","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-84784","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-84785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119212","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-119213","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119214","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-119215","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-119216","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-119217","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-119218","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-119219","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-84786","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119220","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-84787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119221","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-119222","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-119223","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-84788","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-84789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119224","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-84790","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-84791","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119225","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-84792","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119226","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-84793","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119227","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-84794","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119228","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-119229","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-119230","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-119231","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119232","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-119233","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable."}]}],"id":"blk-84795","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119234","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-119235","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-119236","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-119237","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior."}]}],"id":"blk-84797","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119238","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-119239","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-119240","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-119241","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-119242","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-119243","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119244","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-119245","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-84799","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119246","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-119247","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-119248","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-119249","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-119250","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-119251","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-84801","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119252","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-119253","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-119254","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-119255","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-119256","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-119257","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]}],"id":"blk-84803","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119258","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-84806","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119259","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-119260","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-119261","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-84807","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119262","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-84809","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119263","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-84811","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119264","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-84814","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119265","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-84815","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119266","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-119267","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-119268","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-84817","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119269","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-84819","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119270","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-119271","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-119272","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119273","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-119274","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119275","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-119276","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-84821","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84823","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119277","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-84824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119278","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a "},{"id":"spn-119279","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-119280","text":" — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-119281","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-119282","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-84825","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-84826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119283","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-119284","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-119285","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-119286","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-119287","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-119288","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-119289","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-119290","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-84827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119291","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-84828","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119292","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-119293","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-84829","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119294","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-119295","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-84831","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119296","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-119297","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-84833","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119298","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-119299","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-84835","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119300","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-119301","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-119302","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-84838","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119303","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-84839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119304","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-84840","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119305","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-119306","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-84841","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119307","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-119308","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-84843","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119309","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-119310","text":" That's a "},{"id":"spn-119311","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-119312","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-119313","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-119314","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-84845","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119315","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-119316","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-84847","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119317","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-119318","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-119319","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-119320","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-84849","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84851","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119321","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-84852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119322","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-119323","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-119324","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-84853","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119325","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-119326","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-84854","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119327","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-119328","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-84856","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119329","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-119330","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-84858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119331","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-84861","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119332","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-119333","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-84862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119334","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-119335","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-119336","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-119337","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-119338","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119339","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-119340","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119341","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-119342","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119343","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-119344","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-119345","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-119346","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-84863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119347","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-84864","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119348","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-119349","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-119350","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-119351","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-84865","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119352","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-119353","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-84867","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119354","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-119355","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-119356","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-119357","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-84869","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119358","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-119359","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-119360","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-84872","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119361","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-84873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119362","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-84875","spans":[{"id":"spn-119363","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-84876","spans":[{"id":"spn-119364","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-84877","spans":[{"id":"spn-119365","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-84874","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-84878","spans":[{"id":"spn-119366","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-84879","spans":[{"id":"spn-119367","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-84880","spans":[{"id":"spn-119368","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-84881","spans":[{"id":"spn-119369","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-119370","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-84882","spans":[{"id":"spn-119371","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-84883","spans":[{"id":"spn-119372","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-84884","spans":[{"id":"spn-119373","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-119374","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-84885","spans":[{"id":"spn-119375","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-84886","spans":[{"id":"spn-119376","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-84887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119377","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-119378","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-119379","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-84888","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119380","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-84889","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-84890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119381","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-84891","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119382","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-84892","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119383","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-119384","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-119385","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-119386","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact."}]}],"id":"blk-84893","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119387","text":"Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-119388","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-119389","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo."}]}],"id":"blk-84895","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119390","text":"CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-119391","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-119392","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-119393","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-119394","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119395","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-119396","text":" → static HTML."}]}],"id":"blk-84897","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119397","text":"Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]}],"id":"blk-84899","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119398","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-84902","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119399","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-84903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119400","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-119401","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-119402","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-84904","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119403","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-119404","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-119405","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-119406","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-119407","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-119408","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-84905","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119409","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-84907","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119410","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-84909","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119411","text":"These are "},{"id":"spn-119412","marks":["italic"],"text":"integration patterns"},{"id":"spn-119413","text":", not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-84912","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119414","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-84913","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84915","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119415","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-119416","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-84914","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-119418","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-84916","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119419","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-119420","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-119421","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-119422","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-84918","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119423","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-119424","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-84920","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119425","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-84923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119426","marks":["italic"],"text":"This spec is the contract. Everything in `runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md` (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the `supervisor-floor.v1` vocabulary plus the `runefort.dark_factory` reference application — both built on top of this protocol."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierax3bwnmmr4uygfuiz3g3s7g3bf474ori7fg63mg7rty6popn4unzq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}